[size=3][u][b]🛠 Changelog[/b][/u][/size]

[size=3][u][i][0.7.0] - unreleased[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] The command-line checker applies the preferred fixes with `--fix`, and writes SARIF for GitHub code scanning with `--format sarif`.
[*] Quick fixes that create what nothing defines: a cue or library, also in the script [b]md.Script.Cue[/b] names, a label, and a parameter a call passes in the script, order or library it calls.
[*] The README tells where X4CodeSense takes its knowledge from, and what is built in.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A value whose text ends in `name=`, such as [b]comment="… instead of otherobject="[/b] in [b]gs_pirate1.xml[/b] of the Tides of Avarice DLC, is no longer taken for an unclosed value followed by another attribute.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.6.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] The problems of every script and patch in the workspace, not only of the open ones, when [b]x4CodeSense.diagnosticMode[/b] is `workspace`; [b]Choose Which Scripts Show Problems[/b] sets it, also from the status bar's menu.
[*] Apply all preferred fixes in this file: in the light bulb, and as [b]source.fixAll[/b] for `editor.codeActionsOnSave`.
[*] A warning for an AI script name or order id that a call writes as is and no script defines, with a quick fix to the known name it is close to.
[*] The outline shows an order's name as the game shows it.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] After a start of VS Code, the scripts in the restored tabs show their problems, not only the one in front.
[*] X4CodeSense starts with a workspace that holds scripts, before a script is opened.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.5.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Go to Symbol in Workspace: the scripts, cues, libraries and interrupt library items of the game, its DLCs, the extensions and the workspace, also as `md.Script.Cue`.
[*] The parameters of calls (`run_script`, `create_order`, `run_actions`, `<cue ref>`, …): signature help, completion of the parameter names, hover with their description and default, and go to their declaration.
[*] A warning for a parameter a call passes that its target does not declare, with a quick fix to the declared name it is close to. The game's own scripts have four, left behind when a library changed.
[*] AI script names and order ids in calls (`run_script name="'move.generic'"`, `create_order id="'Attack'"`): completion, hover with an order's name and description, go to definition, and find all references, also from [b]<aiscript name>[/b] and `<order id>`.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.4.1] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A patch opened in the group of the diff, such as from the Explorer while the diff has the focus, moves to the patches as before, and now its diff opens below it.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] Typing in large scripts is faster: semantic highlighting takes up to half the time it took, the checks up to a tenth less.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.4.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] Both sides of the diff of a patch have the script's hover, go to definition, references, outline and semantic highlighting, and the side with the patch its completion and quick fixes. That side shows the problems the file before the patch does not have, also what the patch breaks elsewhere in the script.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A folder added to the workspace while the game files are still read is no longer left out of the index until a restart.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.3.0] - 2026-10-01[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Added
[list]
[*] [b]Edit This Patch Above What It Changes[/b]: the patch above the diff of the file it changes, and the caret follows between them. The side with the patch can be edited: typing in what the patch brings in goes into the patch at once; saving the side writes its other changes into the patch as new operations, with full paths, in the order of the places they change.
[*] While the window is arranged so, a file opened in the diff's group moves up to the patch's, and the diff follows the patch in front above.
[/list]
[*] Changed
[list]
[*] In the diff of a patch, what an operation brings in is shown at the column of the element it replaces or is added next to, or one step deeper than the element it is added into, instead of its column in the patch.
[*] A patch's diffs close with the patch.
[/list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] A diff of a patch restored from the last session gets its text once the game files are read.
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][i][0.2.2] - 2026-09-30[/i][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Fixed
[list]
[*] Hover over a property whose name goes on after it, such as [b]mayattack[/b] in `$ship.mayattack.{$faction}`, shows that property and every variant that fits as well. When the type of [b]$ship[/b] was not known, it showed unrelated [b]{$numeric}[/b] properties.
[*] Completion after such a name offers its [b]{…}[/b] variants first, also when the type before it is not known: [b]$ship.mayattack.[/b] offers [b]{$component}[/b] and `{$faction}`.
[*] A bare value such as [b]argon[/b] is taken only where [b]scriptproperties.xml[/b] declares a shortcut for it (`isclass.<classname>`, `skill.<skillname>`), and completion offers bare values only there.
[/list]
[/list]
